```

When `EmptyResultSet` is raised from a child, `empty_needed` decrements. For an AND node with two children (the Exists and the name filter), if Exists raises `EmptyResultSet`, then `empty_needed` becomes 0. The problem is that `~Exists(none)` should logically be `True` (since NOT EXISTS of an empty set is always true), but the current logic doesn't account for the negation of the Exists node itself when handling the exception.

The real issue lies in how `Exists.as_sql()` handles empty querysets.

